; A vowel's level. Per segment three cards in (kind, s, n); per frame snd, V and u (INP at gs, gv, gu); per frame two
; modes and factors out for two mulx machines (OUT at m2, y2 and m3, oy3). A sounding, voiced vowel frame: 708 /
; 1000 (3 dB down) if the vowel is unstressed, then less 30 u / 1000 (it falls off across the vowel). Otherwise
; mode 0 for both.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            seg     INP   kind     03-09: a segment (i counts its frames down)
  04                    INP   s
  05                    INP   i
  06            frm     CLA   i
  07                    SUB   00
  08                    TAC   seg
  09                    STO   i
  10            gs      INP   snd      10-47: a frame: is it a sounding, voiced vowel's
  11            gv      INP   v
  12            gu      INP   u
  13                    CLA   z
  14                    STO   md2
  15                    STO   md3
  16                    STO   y3
  17                    CLA   kind
  18                    SUB   n2
  19                    TAC   vow
  20                    JMP   m2
  21            vow     CLA   snd
  22                    SUB   00
  23                    TAC   m2
  24                    SUB   00
  25                    TAC   on
  26                    JMP   m2
  27            on      CLA   v
  28                    SUB   00
  29                    TAC   m2
  30                    CLA   n2
  31                    STO   md3
  32                    CLA   u
  33                    ADD   u
  34                    ADD   u
  35                    SFT   10
  36                    STO   y3
  37                    CLA   s
  38                    SUB   00
  39                    TAC   un
  40                    JMP   m2
  41            un      CLA   00
  42                    STO   md2
  43            m2      OUT   md2
  44            y2      OUT   c708
  45            m3      OUT   md3
  46            oy3     OUT   y3
  47                    JMP   frm
  50            kind    DATA  0
  51            s       DATA  0
  52            i       DATA  0
  53            snd     DATA  0
  54            v       DATA  0
  55            u       DATA  0
  56            md2     DATA  0
  57            md3     DATA  0
  58            y3      DATA  0
  59            z       DATA  0
  60            n2      DATA  2
  61            c708    DATA  708
